  "body": "Part of #2238 (frame cost: calculate before and cache). Measured with the frame-cost probe of #2238, release build, fig8.step.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe Geometry tab calls `camcraft_app::operation::selection_account` (from `crates/ui/src/egui_app/geo_page.rs`, `body`) on each frame, also when no input changed. It clones the picks and the parameters each time.\n\n| State | Piece | ms per frame (release) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Contour on 10 top edge chains | `ui/properties.op.picks.selection_account` | 4.24 |\n| 2D Adaptive on one welded face | `ui/properties.op.picks.selection_account` | 1.22 |\n\n## Done means\n\n- The notes and the refusal of the selection account are calculated when the picks, the parameters, the setup or the model change, and read from a cache on other frames.\n- The cache is in `app`, next to `selection_account`, so that MCP and the CLI use it too. The key follows `docs/decisions/2238-frame-cost-rule.md` (the input values and the `Arc` of the model features). Do not key it on `doc_version` alone.\n- A counter test: a still frame makes zero new calculations.\n- A changed-input test: a changed pick or parameter gives the new notes, equal to a fresh calculation.\n- The verify check and the generator do not read this cache.\n- The probe `frame_cost_probe` shows the piece under 0.1 ms in release for state b.\n",
